  "body": {
    "id": "thm:kennedy-superclass-private-lower-frontier",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "There is a constant \\(c_K>0\\), depending only on\n\\(d,\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma,L,e_0\\), such that throughout \\(n\\epsilon\\ge1\\),\n\\[\n R_{n,\\epsilon}^{\\mathrm{DP},K}\n \\ge c_K\\left[\n \\left\\{n^{-1/(2+d/\\gamma)}\n \\vee n^{-2/(2+d/\\gamma+d/q)}\\right\\}\n \\vee\\rho_G\\vee\\rho_F\\right].\n\\]\nThis is a converse transfer only; it asserts no upper bound over\n\\(\\mathcal P_K\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "RDPK",
      "d",
      "alpha",
      "beta",
      "gamma",
      "q",
      "L",
      "e0",
      "n",
      "epsilon",
      "rhoG",
      "rhoF"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:privacy-regime",
      "def:frontier-radii",
      "def:kennedy-private-risk",
      "lem:exact-uniform-superclass-monotonicity",
      "lem:nonprivate-cate-rate-floor",
      "thm:full-class-lower-frontier"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "By \\(\\mathrm{lem:exact-uniform-superclass-monotonicity}\\) and\n\\(\\mathrm{thm:full-class-lower-frontier}\\),\n\\[\n R_{n,\\epsilon}^{\\mathrm{DP},K}\n \\ge R_{n,\\epsilon}^{\\mathrm{DP}}\n \\ge c_{\\mathrm{lower}}\n \\{R_n^{\\mathrm{NP}}\\vee\\rho_G\\vee\\rho_F\\}.                 \\tag{12}\n\\]\nThe proved nonprivate floor\n\\(\\mathrm{lem:nonprivate-cate-rate-floor}\\) supplies a constant\n\\(c_{\\mathrm{NP}}>0\\), depending on the same model parameters, for which\n\\[\n R_n^{\\mathrm{NP}}\n \\ge c_{\\mathrm{NP}}\n \\left\\{n^{-1/(2+d/\\gamma)}\n \\vee n^{-2/(2+d/\\gamma+d/q)}\\right\\}.                      \\tag{13}\n\\]\nSubstituting (13) into (12), and using for nonnegative numbers\n\\(u,v,w\\) and \\(a>0\\) the elementary inequality\n\\[\n (au)\\vee v\\vee w\n \\ge (1\\wedge a)(u\\vee v\\vee w),\n\\]\ngives the asserted bound with\n\\(c_K=c_{\\mathrm{lower}}(1\\wedge c_{\\mathrm{NP}})\\).  Every lower branch\ntherefore transfers from the exact-uniform subclass to the larger\nbounded-density class.  No step reverses the inclusion, so the argument\ndoes not transfer any estimator or upper bound.",
    "justification": "The exact-uniform lower construction is a valid subexperiment of the larger bounded-density Hölder class, so all nonprivate, dense-private, and sparse-private converse branches transfer upward without claiming an estimator on that larger class.",
    "gap": "Kennedy et al. establish the nonprivate pointwise-CATE frontier on the bounded-density class but do not provide either pure-private lower branch.",
    "consumer": "The result separates the unconditional superclass converse from the still-open exact-uniform matching upper bound.",
